---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Privacy · TaskDev"
  description="Privacy policy for taskdev.dev"
>
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="muted">What this site collects, in plain terms.</p>

    <h2>Optional analytics</h2>
    <p>
      If you enable analytics, this site loads <a href="https://umami.is/">Umami</a> for anonymous,
      aggregated visit statistics. Umami does not use cookies, does not collect personal data,
      and does not store full IP addresses. Analytics is hosted by Tolbxela.
    </p>
    <p>
      Your analytics preference is stored in browser <code>localStorage</code> under
      <code>taskdev-analytics-consent</code>. If you choose "No thanks", the analytics script is
      not loaded.
    </p>

    <h2>Browser storage</h2>
    <p>This site does not set cookies. It stores only your analytics preference in your browser.</p>

    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>
      The site is hosted on infrastructure operated by Tolbxela. The web server may temporarily
      log request details such as IP address and user agent for security and troubleshooting.
    </p>

    <h2>The TaskDev extension</h2>
    <p>
      The extension itself runs entirely on your machine. Tasks run as local processes, logs
      stay on disk, and TaskDev does not phone home or send any telemetry.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>For privacy questions, email <a class="mail" href="#" data-u="admin" data-h="tolbxela.com" rel="noopener">email</a>.</p>

    <p style="margin-top:2.5rem"><a href="/">← back to taskdev.dev</a></p>
  </article>

  <script is:inline>
    document.querySelectorAll('a.mail').forEach(function (a) {
      var u = a.getAttribute('data-u'), h = a.getAttribute('data-h');
      if (!u || !h) return;
      var addr = u + '@' + h;
      a.setAttribute('href', 'mailto:' + addr);
      a.textContent = addr;
    });
  </script>
</Base>
